<article class="env-definition" id="090L">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/090L">Definition <span data-tag="090L">7.40.2</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{C}$ be a site. </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
We say an object $U$ of $\mathcal{C}$ is <em>weakly contractible</em> if the equivalent conditions of Lemma <a href="/tag/090K" data-tag="090K">7.40.1</a> hold. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
We say a site has <em>enough weakly contractible objects</em> if every object $U$ of $\mathcal{C}$ has a covering $\{ U_ i \to U\} $ with $U_ i$ weakly contractible for all $i$. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
More generally, if $P$ is a property of objects of $\mathcal{C}$ we say that $\mathcal{C}$ has <em>enough $P$ objects</em> if every object $U$ of $\mathcal{C}$ has a covering $\{ U_ i \to U\} $ such that $U_ i$ has $P$ for all $i$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article>